Guard vastnfs's unconditional CC assignment.

Upstream's makefile assigns CC = $(CROSS_COMPILE)gcc unconditionally, and a
makefile assignment beats a value passed in from outside. vastnfs's own DKMS
runner detects the compiler the target kernel was built with (the first token
of LINUX_COMPILER in the kernel's include/generated/compile.h) and passes it
in; without this guard the makefile overwrites that with plain "gcc", which on
Ubuntu HWE kernels is not the compiler that built the kernel.

Verified 2026-09-17 against vastnfs 4.5.9 on aarch64 / 6.17.0-1032-nvidia-64k:
patched builds log CC='aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-13', unpatched log CC='gcc'.

Regenerated against vastnfs 4.5.9; the hunk offset moved from 127 to 132.

--- makefile
+++ makefile.new
@@ -132,11 +132,13 @@
 # compiled with GCC 4.6.0 and above.
 # therefore, to prevent unknown symbol issues we disable function tracing.
 #
+ifndef CC
 ifeq ($(ccache),1)
 CC  = ccache $(CROSS_COMPILE)gcc
 else
 CC  = $(CROSS_COMPILE)gcc
 endif
+endif
 CPP = $(CC) -E

 CPP_MAJOR := $(shell $(CPP) -dumpversion 2>&1 | cut -d'.' -f1)
